==Restrictions==
*Fixed lineup: [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Monk Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] and [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sexy Bathtub Cat]].

==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*6 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Red Cyclone]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage introduces the importance of '''Crowd Control''', as well as the family of enemies known as the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s, which often require heavy crowd-controlling to defeat. Crowd Control units are units that are able to inflict status effects against a specific targetted trait.

You are given a variety of anti-Red/Floating crowd-controllers, and a lot of money is provided in this stage through the Sir Seals, which allow for you to constantly spam your units that will eventually take down the Red Cyclone. It is recommended to prioritize spamming [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cats]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Monk Cat]], as they will be able to perma-[[Freeze]] the Red Cyclone while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]] deals [[Massive Damage]] to it.

==Hints==
The first hint can be viewed within the Enemies Appearing window before beginning the stage. The second only appears as a defeat message when failing it.
*Debuffs like {{Color|Blue|Freeze and Slow}}<br>are an effective solution<br>to Traited enemies.<br>Use units with debuffs that counter<br>Traited enemies to win!
*Many units can inflict debuffs.<br>The more you deploy, the higher your<br>chance of inflicting one on enemies!

